    fields:  # b893
      statement: "hypergumbo subcommands that accept '--input behavior_map.json' must produce a user-readable error and non-zero exit (not a Python traceback) when the file is malformed JSON or has the wrong top-level type."  # b893
      root_cause: "None of the 8 consumers tested (search, explain, symbols, routes, test-coverage, dead-code-maybe, io-boundaries, compact) wrap the json.load() call in a try/except. Malformed JSON: json.JSONDecodeError traceback. Top-level array instead of dict: AttributeError 'list object has no attribute get' at cli.py:1576 (cmd_search) and analogous sites. Same root pattern as INV-zurih (verify-claims YAML traceback). Also: no schema_version validation — a behavior_map with schema_version stripped still 'works', creating a forward-compat trap."  # b893
